# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Particle event R2_LOCLPAR0005, 600 s, in 4 pieces (one component each) built at the attitude of their
# time span (yaw change <= 10 deg per piece); together they make up the event.

# Piece 1 of 4: 0-131.928 s after the event start.
# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/100 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 660 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking +21.87 deg, yaw 5.58 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1.ParticleType 3
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1_beam.dat
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835537550.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_15sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curves (absolute unix times): R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1_lightcurve.dat, R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2_lightcurve.dat, R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3_lightcurve.dat, R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1.Lightcurve File false R2_LOCLPAR0005_p1_lightcurve_shifted.dat

# Piece 2 of 4: 131.928-270.583 s after the event start.
# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/100 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 660 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw 14.65 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2.ParticleType 3
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2_beam.dat
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2.Lightcurve File false R2_LOCLPAR0005_p2_lightcurve_shifted.dat

# Piece 3 of 4: 270.583-423.271 s after the event start.
# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/100 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 660 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw 23.72 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3.ParticleType 3
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3_beam.dat
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3.Lightcurve File false R2_LOCLPAR0005_p3_lightcurve_shifted.dat

# Piece 4 of 4: 423.271-600 s after the event start.
# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/100 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 660 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking +21.88 deg, yaw 32.8 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4.ParticleType 3
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4_beam.dat
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4.Lightcurve File false R2_LOCLPAR0005_p4_lightcurve_shifted.dat
